===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A series of [[interconnected]] rings or [[link]]s usually made of metal.
#: {{ux|en|He wore a gold '''chain''' around the neck.}}
#: {{ux|en|The anchor is connected to the boat with a 100-metre long '''chain'''.}}
# A [[series]] of interconnected things.
#: {{ux|en|a '''chain''' of mountains}}
#: {{ux|en|a '''chain''' of ideas, one leading to the next}}
#: {{ux|en|This led to an unfortunate '''chain''' of events.}}
# A series of stores or [[business]]es with the same [[brand name]].
#: {{ux|en|That '''chain''' of restaurants is expanding into our town.}}
# {{lb|en|organic compound|physical chemistry}} A number of atoms in a series, which combine to form a [[molecule]].
#: {{ux|en|When examined, the molecular '''chain''' included oxygen and hydrogen.}}
# {{lb|en|surveying}} A series of interconnected links of known length, used as a measuring device.
# {{lb|en|surveying}} A long [[measuring tape]].
# A [[unit]] of [[length]], exactly equal to 22 [[yard]]s, 4 [[rod]]s or 100 [[link]]s, and approximately equal to 20.12 [[metre]]s; the length of a {{w|Gunter's chain|Gunter's surveying chain}}; the length of a [[cricket]] [[pitch]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1938|author=w:Xavier Herbert|title=[[w:Capricornia (novel)|Capricornia]]|location=New York|publisher=D. Appleton-Century|year_published=1943|chapter=X|page=177|url=https://archive.org/details/capricornianovel00herb
|passage="But it's too far—must be a quarter of a mile—and I've a portmanteau to carry." {{...}}<br>"Garn!" shouted the guard. "Taint ten '''chain'''. {{...}}"}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics|set theory|order theory}} A [[totally ordered set]], especially a totally ordered subset of a [[poset]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2003|author=Jeremy P. Spinrad|title=Efficient Graph Representations|publisher=w:American Mathematical Society|pageurl=https://books.google.com.au/books?id=RrtXSKMAmWgC&pg=PA108&dq=%22chain%22%7C%22chains%22+%22poset%22&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwj0loivsoncAhXITbwKHfnpAo4Q6AEILDAB#v=onepage&q=%22chain%22%7C%22chains%22%20%22poset%22&f=false|page=108
|passage=We first find an approximation of the '''chain''' partition, i.e. a small but not minimum size set of '''chains''' which cover all elements of the poset.}}
# {{lb|en|algebraic topology|originally}} A [[formal sum]] of [[cell]]s in a [[CW complex]] of a certain [[dimension]] ''k'' (in which case the formal sums are called '''''k''-chains'''); a formal sum of [[simplex|simplices]] or [[cube]]s of a certain dimension in a [[simplical complex]] or [[cubical complex]] (respectively).
# {{lb|en|algebraic topology|[[homological algebra]]|more generally}} An element of a group (or module) in a [[chain complex]].
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[sequence]] of linked [[house]] [[purchase]]s, each of which is [[dependent]] on the preceding and succeeding purchase (said to be "broken" if a buyer or seller [[pull out|pulls out]]).
# That which confines, fetters, or secures; a bond.
#: {{ux|en|the '''chains''' of habit}}
#* {{RQ:Milton Paradise Lost|book=6|passage=Driven down / To '''chains''' of darkness and the undying worm.|year=1873}}
# {{lb|en|nautical|in the plural}} Iron links bolted to the side of a vessel to bold the dead-eyes connected with the shrouds; also, the channels.
# A [[livery collar]], a [[chain of office]].
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=25|passage=And gainſt the General we will lift our ſwords<br>And either lanch his greedie thirſting throat,<br>Or take him priſoner, and his '''chaine''' ſhall ſerue<br>For Manackles, till he be ranſom’d home.}}
# {{lb|en|weaving}} The [[warp]] [[thread]]s of a [[web]].<ref>{{R:Knight AMD}}</ref>

