===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fasten]] something with a chain.
#: {{ux|en|You should '''chain''' your bicycle to the railings to protect it from being stolen.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To connect as if with a chain, due to dependence, addiction, or other feelings
#: {{ux|en|Sometimes I feel like I'm '''chained''' to this computer.}}
#: {{ux|en|She's been '''chained''' to her principles since she was 18, it's unlikely you can convince her otherwise.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[link]] multiple items together.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[secure]] someone with [[fetter]]s.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[obstruct]] the mouth of a [[river]] etc with a chain.
# {{lb|en|figurative}} To [[obligate]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=August 13, 2017| author=Brandon Nowalk| title=Oldtown offers one last game-changing secret as Game Of Thrones goes behind enemy lines (newbies)| work=The Onion AV Club| url=http://www.avclub.com/tvclub/oldtown-offers-one-last-game-changing-secret-game--259407| passage= I miss when Game Of Thrones was wide open, but even then, the writers were '''chained''' to a narrative they didn’t yet know the ending of and feared straying too far from. }}
# {{lb|en|computing}} To relate [[data]] items with a chain of [[pointer]]s.
# {{lb|en|computing}} To be chained to another data item.
#* {{quote-web|en|date=January 15, 2016|site=Medium|author=Mark Papadakis|title=Coroutines and Fibers. Why and When|url=https://medium.com/software-development-2/coroutines-and-fibers-why-and-when-5798f08464fd|passage=You don’t need to maintain state, or partition execution into different objects that then you can '''chain''' together (one executes the other on completion — '''chained''' continuations).}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[measure]] a distance using a 66-[[foot]] long chain, as in land [[surveying]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1887|author=Harriet W. Daly|title=Digging, Squatting, and Pioneering Life in the Northern Territory of South Australia|page=99|passage=As the line was surveyed - a sufficient length being first '''chained''' by a surveyor, who was followed by axemen - trees had to be felled and a certain width maintained, which was specified in the contract, for drays had to follow, and the trees might have fallen upon the line and broken it down at the very outset.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|computing|rare|associated with {{w|Acorn Computers}}}} To load and automatically run (a program).
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=1996|author=Mr D Walsh|title=Running two programs from a batch file|newsgroup=comp.sys.acorn.misc
|passage=How do you get one program to '''chain''' another? I want to run DrawWorks2 then !Draw but as soon as you run Drawworks2 it finishes the batch file and doesn't go on to the next instruction! Is there a way without loading one of these automatic loaders?}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=1998|author=Juan Flynn|title=BBC software transmitted on TV - how to load?|newsgroup=comp.sys.acorn.misc
|passage=You can do LOAD "" or CHAIN "" to load or '''chain''' the next program if I remember correctly (it's been a loooong time since I've used a tape on an Acorn!)}}
#* {{quote-newsgroup|en|year=2006|author=Richard Porter|title=SpamStamp double headers|newsgroup=comp.sys.acorn.apps
|passage=Recent versions of AntiSpam no longer use the Config file but have a Settings file instead, so when I updated the Config file to '''chain''' SpamStamp it had no effect as it was a redundant file.}}

